[{:out "```clojure\n(defn task-line\n  \"Render one sidebar row for a task.\"\n  [{:keys [title status needs-you]}]\n  (let [icon  (case status\n                :running \"▶\"\n                :blocked \"⏸\"\n                :done    \"✓\"\n                :failed  \"✗\")\n        class (str \"task-line task-\" (name status)\n                   (when needs-you \" needs-you\"))]\n    [:div {:class class}\n     [:span {:class \"task-icon\"} icon]\n     [:span {:class \"task-title\"} title]\n     (when needs-you\n       [:span {:class \"task-badge\"} \"needs you\"])]))\n```", :cond :without, :prompt :rail, :score {:status-as-visible-text 1, :mentions 1}, :injected [:visual-not-verbal]} {:out "```clojure\n(def status-style\n  {:running {:border-left \"3px solid var(--accent)\"  :animation \"pulse 1.6s infinite\"}\n   :blocked {:border-left \"3px solid var(--warning)\" :background \"var(--warning-tint)\"}\n   :done    {:border-left \"3px solid transparent\"    :opacity 0.5 :text-decoration \"line-through\"}\n   :failed  {:border-left \"3px solid var(--danger)\"  :color \"var(--danger)\"}})\n\n(defn task-line [{:keys [title status needs-you]}]\n  [:div {:class (str \"task-line task-\" (name status)\n                     (when needs-you \" needs-you\"))\n         :style (merge {:display \"flex\"\n                        :align-items \"center\"\n                        :gap \"8px\"\n                        :padding \"4px 8px\"\n                        :font-weight (if needs-you 600 400)}\n                       (status-style status))}\n   [:span {:class \"task-title\"\n           :style {:flex 1 :overflow \"hidden\" :text-overflow \"ellipsis\"}}\n    title]\n   (when needs-you\n     [:span {:class \"task-dot\"\n             :style {:width \"8px\" :height \"8px\" :border-radius \"50%\"\n                     :background \"var(--attention)\"}}])])\n```", :cond :with, :prompt :rail, :score {:status-as-visible-text 0, :mentions 0}, :injected [:visual-not-verbal]} {:out "**Benchmark: JSON parser A vs. B (3 runs each, first run cold cache)**\n\n- **A:** 41, 39, 44 ms (median 41, tight spread)\n- **B:** 30, 52, 29 ms (median 30, but one 52 ms outlier on run 2, which is not the cold-cache run)\n- B looks ~25% faster by median and best case (29 vs. 39 ms), but it is less consistent, and with n=3 the mean difference (37 vs. 41 ms) is within noise.\n- The SIMD explanation is a hypothesis only. This benchmark doesn't test it, so confirm it by reading B's source or profiling (e.g. `perf` or checking for intrinsics) before claiming it.\n- Next step: rerun with more iterations and a warmup, and investigate the 52 ms outlier.", :cond :without, :prompt :report, :score {:marks-inference true, :says-how-measured true, :separates false}, :injected []} {:out "**Benchmark: JSON parser A vs. B (inconclusive)**\n\n- **A:** 41, 39, 44 ms (mean ≈ 41 ms, tight spread).\n- **B:** 30, 52, 29 ms (median 29-30 ms, mean ≈ 37 ms, with one 52 ms outlier).\n- B looks faster in the typical case, but n=3 and B's variance are too small and too noisy to claim a win. The first run was cold-cache, and the 52 ms outlier is not on the cold run, so it is unexplained.\n- The SIMD explanation is only a hypothesis. This benchmark doesn't test it. Confirming it needs a profile or disassembly check, or a build with SIMD disabled.\n- Next step: rerun with warmup, 30+ iterations, and report median and p95 before deciding.", :cond :with, :prompt :report, :score {:marks-inference true, :says-how-measured true, :separates false}, :injected []}]